Glory of Rome <version>
=======================

Glory of Rome is a turn-based fantasy strategy game: raise an army, hunt the
villains who have carved up Italia, and deliver them to the Senate before
your commission runs out. It runs on OpenBounty, an open-source engine, and
everything it needs is in this folder -- there is nothing else to download.


INSTALL

  Linux:    extract the tarball and run ./openbounty
  Windows:  extract the zip and double-click openbounty.exe
  macOS:    extract the zip; first launch will be blocked by Gatekeeper.
            Right-click openbounty in Finder, choose Open, then click
            Open in the dialog. Or, from a terminal:
              xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine ./openbounty

  Keep the assets folder next to the program: the game is in it.


CONTROLS

  Arrow keys or the numeric keypad move; Enter chooses; Esc opens the game
  menu, where every command lives. A gamepad works too.


MORE

  Source, issues and releases: https://github.com/dannyheskett/openbounty
